<simplesect kind="return"><para>Response body on success, <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput> on any failure. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>All exceptions (init failure, unsupported method, cURL error, empty body) are caught internally, logged via Message and converted to <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput>; nothing is thrown to the caller. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para><computeroutput>data</computeroutput> is passed to libcurl by pointer, so it must outlive the call; this holds for normal synchronous use. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
